1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,900
This is Stealth Checkout, a payment box you drop into any website.

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:08,600
Someone pays you privately. The chain never learns who.

3
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:13,900
Starknet could already send money privately. Receiving it? Nobody built that.

4
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:16,000
So we did.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,238
Here's our demo shop: an arcade that sells game credits.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,646
That panel is the whole widget. One call drops it into any page.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,662
No wallet, no install. Drop a coin in.

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,510
The shop's server saw the payment and granted the credit. Payment in, product out.

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,486
Now look at the price before you sign.

10
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:45,538
A one STRK coin costs seven.

11
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:54,000
STRK20's pool takes six every single time. Flat. Doesn't matter if you move one or a thousand.

12
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,158
That number is nowhere in STRK20's docs. We read it off the contract ourselves.

13
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:08,646
So a private payment has a minimum practical size. Under sixty STRK, fees eat more than ten percent.

14
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:14,054
This panel spells out what the payment leaks. Including the parts we couldn't hide.

15
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:20,286
Merchant side. Every invoice gets a link and a QR.

16
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:27,054
Or print one code and stick it on the counter. The customer picks the amount.

17
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:34,342
One printed code means one address forever. Anyone can add up your sales.

18
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:41,386
Your customers stay anonymous either way. We tell you that before you choose.

19
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:48,942
The QR encoder is ours. No dependencies, checked against the ISO spec.

20
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,342
Mainnet now. Real money.

21
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:01,310
See the warning? Nothing here has checked this link's amount or address. We print that in red instead of hiding it.

22
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:07,270
A link can't vouch for itself. So there's no box here for naming your own auditor.

23
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,462
Signing. The pool submits it, so the chain never records me as the sender.

24
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:21,226
The merchant's server picks it up over public RPC. No wallet open anywhere.

25
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:28,370
It counts what came in, not what's sitting there. Money already on the address proves nothing.

26
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:35,366
Signed webhook fires, the invoice flips to paid, and the order goes out.

27
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Real mainnet transactions, all verified. Over two hundred tests. Nine rounds of tearing it apart.

28
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:48,070
And the README also says what those transactions don't prove.

29
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:58,246
Stealth Checkout, the receiving side of STRK20. MIT licensed. Drop it into your app, and get paid.
